===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰerǵʰ-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|bourgeois||a class of citizens who were wealthier members of the Third Estate}}, from {{der|en|fro|borgeis|burgeis|t=town dweller}}, from {{der|en|frk|*burg}}, ultimately from {{der|en|gem-pro|*burgz||stronghold; city}} (whence {{m|en|borough}}). {{doublet|en|burgess}}; compare also {{m|en|burgish}}.

